H4902G.def:
A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Genèse 10:2; 
son of: Japheth (H3315); 
brother of: Gomer (H1586), Magog (H4031), Madai (H4074), Javan (H3120), Tubal (H8422) and Tiras (H8494)
§ Mesech or Meshech = "drawing out"
1) son of Japheth, grandson of Noah, and progenitor of peoples to the north of Israel
1a) descendants of Mesech often mentioned in connection with Tubal, Magog, and other northern nations including the Moschi, a people on the borders of Colchis and Armenia

H4902J.def:
A man of the Syrians living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Genèse 10:23; 
son of: Aram (H0758); 
brother of: Uz (H5780), Hul (H2343) and Gether (H1666); also called Meshech at 1 Chroniques 1:17; 
Another name of mash (מַשׁ "Mash" H4851)
§ Mesech or Meshech = "drawing out"
1) son of Japheth, grandson of Noah, and progenitor of peoples to the north of Israel
1a) descendants of Mesech often mentioned in connection with Tubal, Magog, and other northern nations including the Moschi, a people on the borders of Colchis and Armenia

H4919H.def:
A man of the tribe of Levi living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at 1 Chroniques 9:12; 
son of: Immer (H0564); 
father of: Meshullam (H4918M); also called Meshillemoth at Néhémie 11:13;
Another name of me.shil.le.mit (מְשִׁלֵּמִית "Meshillemith" H4921)
§ Meshillemoth = "recompense"
1) an Ephraimite, one of the chiefs of the tribe in the reign of king Pekah of Israel
1a) also 'Meshillemith'
2) a priest, son of Immer
2a) also 'Meshillemith'

H4920.def:
A man of the tribe of Levi living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at 1 Chroniques 9:21; 
father of: Zechariah (H2148A), Jediael (H3043J), Zebadiah (H2069J), Jathniel (H3496), Elam (H5867H), Jehohanan (H3076I) and Eliehoenai (H0454A); also called Shelemiah at 1 Chroniques 26:14;
Also named: she.lem.yah (שֶׁלֶמְיָהוּ "Shelemiah" H8018O) 
§ Meshelemiah = "whom Jehovah repays"
a Korhite Levite porter or gatekeeper of the house of God in the time of David

H4921.def:
A man of the tribe of Levi living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at 1 Chroniques 9:12; 
son of: Immer (H0564); 
father of: Meshullam (H4918M); also called Meshillemoth at Néhémie 11:13;
Also named: me.shil.le.mot (מְשִׁלֵּמוֹת "Meshillemoth" H4919H) 
§ Meshillemith = "recompense"
a priest, son of Immer. See also 'Meshillemoth'

H4922.def:
A woman living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2 Rois 21:19; 
daughter of: Haruz (H2743); married to Manasseh (H4519H); 
mother of: Amon (H0526H) 
§ Meshullemeth = "friend"
daughter of Haruz of Jotbah, wife of king Manasseh of Judah, and mother of king Amon of Judah

H4927G.def:
A man of the Arabs living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Genèse 25:14; 
son of: Ishmael (H3458); 
brother of: Nebaioth (H5032), Kedar (H6938), Adbeel (H0110), Mibsam (H4017), Dumah (H1746), Massa (H4854), Hadad (H2301), Tema (H8485), Jetur (H3195), Naphish (H5305), Kedemah (H6929) and Mahalath (H4258)
§ Mishma = "a hearing"
1) one of the 12 sons of Ishmael
2) son of Mibsam of the family of Simeon

H4927H.def:
A man of the tribe of Simeon living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1 Chroniques 4:25; 
son of: Mibsam (H4017H); 
father of: Hammuel (H2536)
§ Mishma = "a hearing"
1) one of the 12 sons of Ishmael
2) son of Mibsam of the family of Simeon

H4936.def:
A man of the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1 Chroniques 8:12; 
son of: Elpaal (H0508); 
brother of: Eber (H5677I), Shemed (H8106B), Beriah (H1283I), Shema (H8087I), Zebadiah (H2069H), Meshullam (H4918J), Hizki (H2395), Heber (H2268J), Ishmerai (H3461), Izliah (H3152) and Jobab (H3103K) 
§ Misham = "purification"
a Benjamite, son of Elpaal and descendant of Shaharaim

H4967.def:
A man living at the time before the Flood, first mentioned at Genèse 4:18; 
son of: Mehujael (H4232); 
father of: Lamech (H3929) 
§ Methusael = "who is of God"
son of Mehujael, 4th in descent from Cain, and father of Lamech

H4968.def:
A man living at the time before the Flood, first mentioned at Genèse 5:21; 
son of: Enoch (H2585H); 
father of: Lamech (H3929H)
Also named: Mathousala (Μαθουσάλα "Methuselah" G3103) 
§ Methuselah = "man of the dart"
son of Enoch, 6th in descent from Seth, and father of Lamech
